{"lines":[{"h":0.01453488398216074,"y":0.097383720789796402,"x":0.10288065376424878,"w":0.36419754028320311,"c":1,"t":"Charles's adventures after losing the Battle of"},{"h":0.011627907185728703,"c":1,"x":0.102880660055007,"t":"Worcester hide the uncomfortable truth that","y":0.11482558128722287,"w":0.34979423522949216},{"y":0.13221436959434918,"x":0.10288066366528284,"t":"whilst almost everyone in England had been","w":0.35390945434570309,"h":0.013250883392226243,"c":1},{"t":"appalled by the execution of his father, they","w":0.34979423522949216,"c":1,"h":0.014723203769140158,"y":0.14811542992341609,"x":0.10082304688022195},{"h":0.010174418787512574,"c":1,"y":0.16569767432409077,"t":"had not welcomed the arrival of his son with","x":0.10288065911326233,"w":0.35596707661946614},{"x":0.10082304956014507,"w":0.36008229573567707,"t":"the Scots army, but had instead firmly bolted","h":0.01453659587810685,"y":0.18168433448086574,"c":1},{"t":"their doors. This was partly because he rode at","x":0.098765429938209387,"y":0.19758539482460657,"w":0.37448560078938797,"c":1,"h":0.014723203769140158},{"t":"the head of what looked like a foreign invasion","h":0.01773601033241079,"y":0.21332909495582408,"x":0.098668310724821892,"c":1,"w":0.37880544026692708},{"x":0.10082305128463773,"y":0.23110465102806954,"c":1,"w":0.37654319763183597,"t":"force and partly because, after almost a decade","h":0.01453488398216074},{"c":1,"x":0.10288065645268811,"h":0.013100227562642619,"y":0.24852767952764254,"w":0.34567901611328122,"t":"of civil war, people were desperate to avoid"},{"t":"it beginning again. This makes it all the more","c":1,"x":0.10288065833929466,"y":0.26295641927051827,"h":0.014723203769140047,"w":0.36008229573567707},{"y":0.28197674406445528,"w":0.34773661295572916,"x":0.10082305144077082,"h":0.013081395583944722,"c":1,"t":"interesting that Charles II himself loved the"},{"w":0.35390945434570309,"t":"story so much ever after. As well as retelling","h":0.013081395583944722,"y":0.29796511615551535,"x":0.10288066370569264,"c":1},{"c":1,"h":0.014723203769140047,"w":0.34773661295572916,"y":0.3138987041939143,"t":"it to anyone who would listen, causing eye-","x":0.10082305137150972},{"h":0.01472320376914027,"c":1,"y":0.33127208489262583,"t":"rolling among courtiers, he set in train a series","x":0.098765429955731371,"w":0.37448560078938797},{"w":0.35390945434570309,"t":"of initiatives to memorialise it. There was to","h":0.013081395583944722,"c":1,"x":0.10082305046831418,"y":0.34738372080731761},{"h":0.015991795610623361,"x":0.098765437301371953,"w":0.36625513712565111,"y":0.36336866888783226,"t":"be a new order of chivalry, the Knights of the","c":1},{"x":0.10082304764861713,"w":0.37242797851562504,"h":0.014723203769140158,"c":1,"t":"Royal Oak. A series of enormous oil paintings","y":0.38074204922970301},{"c":1,"y":0.39680232543235339,"x":0.10082304671165768,"h":0.016036308275094724,"t":"depicting the episode were produced, including","w":0.37860081990559891},{"c":1,"w":0.35390945434570309,"h":0.013081395583944611,"y":0.41424418592327039,"t":"a two-metre-wide canvas of Boscobel Wood","x":0.10082305055124939},{"t":"and a set of six similarly enormous paintings","h":0.016008916255020766,"c":1,"x":0.10082304499668093,"w":0.36213991800944012,"y":0.43021201411554455},{"x":0.10069497117541289,"y":0.44585224667851953,"c":1,"h":0.018324482426907318,"w":0.33768730163574218,"t":"of the king on the run. In 1660, Charles II"},{"y":0.46366279056183068,"h":0.01454686781542891,"c":1,"t":"commissioned the artist John Michael Wright","w":0.36831275939941399,"x":0.10082304408644921},{"x":0.098765429469303945,"w":0.38065844217936196,"y":0.47965116262037366,"t":"to paint a flying squadron of cherubs* carrying","h":0.01598837238037687,"c":1},{"h":0.016026036337772775,"c":1,"x":0.098765429963957554,"y":0.4970553591494471,"t":"an oak tree to the heavens on the ceiling of his","w":0.37448560078938803},{"w":0.36831275939941405,"c":1,"h":0.016195524146054185,"x":0.098765430861042489,"t":"bedchamber. It is hard to imagine many other","y":0.51295641949194337},{"x":0.098765435441213037,"w":0.366255137125651,"h":0.01453488398216074,"c":1,"t":"kings marking the lowest point in their life so","y":0.53052325567882441},{"t":"enthusiastically, or indeed pulling off such an","x":0.10063639432961419,"w":0.36459587097167961,"h":0.020009490149040743,"y":0.54374062461464667,"c":1},{"t":"escape in the first place.","x":0.10055205638243574,"y":0.56116758833567482,"h":0.019211684857156186,"w":0.19591332753499346,"c":1},{"y":0.59593023239285681,"t":"Charles Spencer is the perfect person to","c":1,"w":0.31893002827962241,"h":0.01598837238037687,"x":0.10082305145634052},{"c":1,"t":"pass the story on to a new generation. His","h":0.017834196101931155,"x":0.10065939387763066,"y":0.6129402440103856,"w":0.33571225484212236},{"t":"* cherub: an image of angelic children used in paintings","c":1,"x":0.10068691510511812,"y":0.84589231740011184,"w":0.3129774983723958,"h":0.013017876830623276},{"c":0.30000001192092896,"t":"1718867188","x":0.7716049391467531,"h":0.008720930389296444,"w":0.069958845774332645,"y":0.046511627815394085},{"h":0.017632177777509361,"c":1,"x":0.49985360891247088,"y":0.097312339416676163,"w":0.34393160502115883,"t":"pacey, readable prose steers deftly clear of"},{"c":1,"h":0.01598837238037687,"t":"modern idioms and elegantly brings to life the","x":0.50000000241984921,"y":0.11482558124556963,"w":0.37242797851562492},{"t":"details of the great tale. He has even-handed","x":0.50000000068263473,"w":0.35596707661946614,"c":1,"y":0.13221436958142285,"h":0.014723203769140158},{"w":0.34979423522949227,"h":0.014723203769140047,"c":1,"x":0.50000000175621206,"t":"sympathy for both the fugitive king and the","y":0.14811542989600479},{"y":0.16424418623529391,"x":0.50205761768695012,"h":0.014534882858869502,"c":1,"t":"fierce republican regime that hunted him,","w":0.33127571105957032},{"x":0.50197238862953675,"c":1,"y":0.18009433772557149,"h":0.01500906848795136,"t":"and he succeeds in his desire to explore far","w":0.34584754943847662},{"x":0.50000000441489989,"w":0.33127571105957032,"c":1,"y":0.19758539480658643,"h":0.016195524146054185,"t":"more of the background of the story than"},{"y":0.21511627893424179,"t":"previous books on the subject have done. Indeed,","w":0.37860081990559891,"c":1,"x":0.50000000149058832,"h":0.014565699794126696},{"y":0.22970160320163746,"c":1,"x":0.4998665190688043,"t":"the opening third of the book is about how","w":0.343878428141276,"h":0.01652658617538616},{"c":1,"t":"Charles II found himself at Worcester in the first","y":0.24558303860409569,"w":0.37860081990559902,"h":0.016044867754824943,"x":0.50205761736201526},{"t":"place, which for some will be reason alone to","w":0.36435803731282546,"x":0.50195187941166775,"y":0.2632464375174326,"c":1,"h":0.014621704851921047},{"x":0.49967955258914143,"t":"read To Catch a King.","w":0.18185026804606119,"h":0.017701070356425208,"c":1,"y":0.2792245889609698},{"x":0.49999999785092009,"c":1,"t":"The tantalising question left, in the end, is that","w":0.37448560078938808,"y":0.31389870418359345,"h":0.016043156420524673},{"y":0.32983027145288368,"t":"of what it all meant. Would Charles II have","w":0.34588597615559902,"c":1,"h":0.015601796171550109,"x":0.49990673279192832},{"w":0.37860081990559902,"x":0.50205761461617759,"t":"been a different king had these six weeks never","h":0.013081395583944722,"y":0.34738372080840385,"c":1},{"t":"happened? The days and nights spent in hiding","x":0.50000000601352612,"w":0.37654319763183597,"h":0.01453488398216074,"c":1,"y":0.36482558126053266},{"t":"must have affected him in some way. Did the","x":0.49999999977499632,"y":0.38074204922885113,"w":0.36213991800944012,"h":0.014723203769140047,"c":1},{"y":0.39680232544593508,"w":0.37860081990559891,"t":"need to assume disguises, to survive on wit and","h":0.014563987898180697,"c":1,"x":0.50205761463293441},{"h":0.01598837238037687,"w":0.37037038167317704,"t":"charm alone, to use trickery and subterfuge to","y":0.41424418589760981,"x":0.49999999423293995,"c":1},{"t":"escape from tight corners help form him? This","c":1,"w":0.37448560078938803,"y":0.43021201412936527,"x":0.49999999787440835,"h":0.014555427856804748},{"y":0.44337245996394692,"w":0.38110832214355478,"x":0.49978199944890461,"t":"is the one area where the book doesn't quite hit","h":0.01949077107459829,"c":1},{"x":0.49999999426429165,"c":1,"t":"the mark. Instead its depiction of Charles II in","h":0.014546867815428799,"y":0.46366279056201232,"w":0.37037038167317715},{"h":0.018622912843881734,"w":0.38289212544759116,"c":1,"y":0.47952386637582234,"t":"his final years as an ineffective, pleasure-loving","x":0.49991577720777097},{"w":0.37681083679199223,"y":0.49604301115734772,"t":"monarch doesn't do justice to the man (neither","c":1,"h":0.017095516371080977,"x":0.49987314601778299},{"y":0.51295641950782234,"w":0.33127571105957032,"t":"is it accurate), or to the complexity of his","h":0.014723203769140158,"x":0.50205761760856493,"c":1},{"x":0.50000000149210222,"w":0.37860081990559902,"y":0.5305232556643551,"h":0.016002068109591039,"t":"character. But this one niggle aside, To Catch a","c":1},{"y":0.54651162775488504,"t":"King is an excellent read, and those who come","c":1,"x":0.50205760732455507,"h":0.01598837238037687,"w":0.37037038167317715},{"x":0.49986907131370589,"y":0.56202993544361513,"t":"to it knowing little of the famous tale will find","w":0.3726646931966146,"h":0.017890237105047113,"c":1},{"c":1,"x":0.5020576123062197,"t":"they have a treat in store.","y":0.57979976436460745,"w":0.20370370229085288,"h":0.014723203769140158},{"y":0.86773255796252025,"t":"25","x":0.8580246914705375,"c":1,"h":0.013081395583944722,"w":0.024691357612609877},{"t":"IELTSXpress.com","c":1,"y":0.95311055968589831,"w":0.30613845825195307,"x":0.66991094639740412,"h":0.033792529426278195}],"w":2400,"h":3395}